// Rule: [T1036.005] Nik C2 - Csrss Non SYSTEM32 Execution
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1036.005
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Production candidate for csrss non system32 execution, with evidence boundaries and target-environment validation requirements
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for csrss non system32 execution using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: NIK C2 / system-process masquerading Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceProcessEvents A match proves only that a process named csrss.exe executed outside the canonical Windows System32 path.
// A match does not prove: It does not establish NIK C2 attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// NIK C2 / system-process masquerading
// Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceProcessEvents
// A match proves only that a process named csrss.exe executed outside the
// canonical Windows System32 path. It does not establish NIK C2 attribution.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "csrss.exe"
| where not(FolderPath startswith @"C:\Windows\System32\")
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    AccountName,
    FileName,
    FolderPath,
    SHA1,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    ProcessIntegrityLevel,
    ProcessTokenElevation,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    ProcessId,
    ProcessUniqueId,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
